  "cil_liability": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. Furthermore, the applicant fails to indicate that the home will be provided for children and young people who meet this threshold i.e. being a specialist and can demonstrate experience of managing complex young people and those with disabilities, thus would not meet the current needs of LBBD Children’s Social Care, as confirmed by LBBD&#x27;s Lead Commissioner in Children&#x27;s Social Care.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&amp;nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework (August 2026) Policy D7, H1, H12 and S2 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies SP3 and SPDG1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposed outbuilding, by reason of its design and excessive scale, presents a dominant feature that is not subservient to the main dwelling and results in an overdevelopment of the modest site as well as compromising the openness of the characteristic corner plot at which it is situated.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;, This is notably given the location of the application site within the Becontree Estate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;As such, the proposed development is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (August 2026) - Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021) - Policies CP2 and CP3 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010) - Policies BP2, BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011) - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) - Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD4 and DMD6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ]
}